 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 534167,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the perimeter of a square table that measures 30 inches across from one side to its opposite side.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The formula for the perimeter <i>P</i> for a rectangle with length <i>L</i> and width <i>W</i> is <span data-math=\"P = 2L + 2W\"></span>.</p>\n<p> A square is a rectangle whose length and width have equal measures.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"P = 2L + 2W = 2\\left( {30{\\rm{\\ in}}} \\right) + 2\\left( {30{\\rm{\\ in}}} \\right) = 60{\\rm{\\ in}} + 60{\\rm{ in = }}120{\\rm{\\ in}}\"></span></p>\n<p>The perimeter is 120 inches.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "120 in"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
